    },
    {
      "id": "413e611a-75ae-46e2-bd4a-01931c632f95",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 1,
      "content": "ABOUT THE MAJOR The social work and social welfare majors prepare students for positions in a variety of social work service careers. The majors integrate theory and practice, instill an understanding of the relationship between social services and Christian faith, and encourage a commitment to social justice and a life of service. It does so in the context of a liberal arts education informed by a Christian worldview. Upon completion of the majors, students will be prepared to seek entry level employment or pursue advanced study in the field per requirements specific to their matriculating institution. Students complete a set of foundational and advanced courses in human development, social policy, social work methods, practice and research. **Agreement does not include all required courses for the major at FPU** This agreement lists courses that are prerequisites or may be completed prior to transfer to satisfy major requirements. All transfer courses must be completed with a grade of C- or better, and students must complete a minimum of 18 units in the major at FPU. Please contact an academic advisor to discuss the recommended sequence of courses, including courses that may count for both GE and major requirements. To view the full degree requirements, please refer to the Undergraduate Catalog: https://catalog.fresno.edu/index.php .",
      "contentHtml": "<p><strong style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(22, 43, 132);\">ABOUT THE MAJOR</strong></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The social work and social welfare majors prepare students for positions in a variety of social work service careers. The majors integrate theory and practice, instill an understanding of the relationship between social services and Christian faith, and encourage a commitment to social justice and a life of service. It does so in the context of a liberal arts education informed by a Christian worldview. Upon completion of the majors, students will be prepared to seek entry level employment or pursue advanced study in the field per requirements specific to their matriculating institution. Students complete a set of foundational and advanced courses in human development, social policy,&nbsp;social work methods, practice and research.</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(169, 62, 58);\">﻿**Agreement does not include all required courses for the major at FPU**</strong></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">This agreement lists courses that are prerequisites or may be completed prior to transfer to satisfy major requirements. All transfer courses must be completed with a grade of C- or better, and students must complete a minimum of 18 units in the major at FPU. Please contact an academic advisor to discuss the recommended sequence of courses, including courses that may count for both GE and major requirements.&nbsp;To view the full degree requirements, please refer to the Undergraduate Catalog: </span><a href=\"https://catalog.fresno.edu/index.php\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px;\">https://catalog.fresno.edu/index.php</a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">.</span></p>"
    }
